.policy "ruff-n813-camelcase-imported-as-lowercase" revision 2
.description "Keep the alias of an imported CamelCase name in CamelCase; a lowercase alias makes readers mistake a class for a function or variable."
.language python
.mode steer
.scope include "**/*"

// Ruff N813 (pep8-naming): a CamelCase name imported under an all-lowercase alias. Names are read as Ruff's parser
// reads them, NFKC-normalised, and cased by Unicode's Uppercase/Lowercase. Exempt when the name or the alias matches
// `pep8-naming.ignore-names`.
//   from mod import CamelCase as camelcase    ← N813
//   from mod import ǅx as dzx                 ← N813: the name is "Džx"
//   from m import Ǳ as dz                     not reported: the name is "DZ"
#include "python/python-20.rerail"

.violation N813(at: node, x: symbol, a: symbol) code "N813"
    "Use a CamelCase alias instead of `{a}` for `{x}` and update its uses; leave it if `{x}` is really a function or variable despite its CamelCase name."
    suppress ruff "N813"
N813(i, x, a) :- ruff_alias_import(i, x, a), ruff_camel(i, x), ruff_cased_lower(i, a), !ruff_ignored(i, x),
    !ruff_ignored(i, a).
